            <div xml:id="d235-a1">

                <pb facs="0581" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg485"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Governor-General Lorne to Sir Edward
                        Thornton.</hi></head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your dispatch No. 58, of
                    the 21st November, addressed to General Sir Patrick McDougall, inclosing a copy
                    of a note from the Secretary of State of the United States complaining of the
                    forcible removal of the American steamtug Crusader from a United States port,
                    when in charge of officers of justice, and carried be Port Sarnia, Ontario, I
                    have the honor of transmitting to you herewith, for the information of the
                    United States Government, a copy of an approved report of the privy council on
                    the subject, to which is appended a copy of a report of the collector of customs
                    at Sarnia, who was instructed to make full inquiries into the circumstances of
                    the case.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>LORNE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
